From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mikhail Tsukerman <miketsukerman@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 10:36:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Kconfig: add a Linux DRM rendering backend choice

v9.4.0 implements GBM buffers (LV_USE_LINUX_DRM_GBM_BUFFERS) and EGL
rendering (LV_LINUX_DRM_USE_EGL) in the Linux DRM driver, and
lv_conf_internal.h reads both from CONFIG_ symbols, but Kconfig does not
define them, so they cannot be enabled in a Kconfig-based build.

Add a "Linux DRM rendering backend" choice selecting them, modelled on
the equivalent choice in LVGL master. The EGL backend also selects
LV_USE_OPENGLES; LV_USE_EGL is derived from LV_LINUX_DRM_USE_EGL in
lv_conf_internal.h.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [v9.4.x only; LVGL master already provides an equivalent "Rendering backend" choice]
Signed-off-by: Mikhail Tsukerman <miketsukerman@gmail.com>
---
 Kconfig | 37 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 37 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Kconfig b/Kconfig
index 5d05e0c..efb0195 100644
--- a/Kconfig
+++ b/Kconfig
@@ -2069,6 +2069,43 @@ menu "LVGL configuration"
 			bool "Use Linux DRM device"
 			default n
 
+		choice
+			prompt "Linux DRM rendering backend"
+			depends on LV_USE_LINUX_DRM
+			default LV_LINUX_DRM_BACKEND_FBDEV
+			help
+				Select how the Linux DRM driver presents rendered frames.
+
+			config LV_LINUX_DRM_BACKEND_FBDEV
+				bool "Dumb buffers (no GPU)"
+				help
+					Software rendering into DRM/KMS dumb buffers.
+
+			config LV_LINUX_DRM_BACKEND_GBM
+				bool "GBM DMA buffers"
+				select LV_USE_LINUX_DRM_GBM_BUFFERS
+				help
+					Use MESA GBM for Linux DRM DMA buffers. Requires linking
+					with libgbm.
+
+			config LV_LINUX_DRM_BACKEND_EGL
+				bool "EGL (OpenGL ES, hardware-accelerated)"
+				select LV_LINUX_DRM_USE_EGL
+				select LV_USE_OPENGLES
+				help
+					Render via OpenGL ES 2.0 and EGL on a GBM surface.
+					Requires libgbm; libEGL and libGLESv2 are loaded at
+					runtime.
+		endchoice
+
+		config LV_USE_LINUX_DRM_GBM_BUFFERS
+			bool
+			depends on LV_USE_LINUX_DRM
+
+		config LV_LINUX_DRM_USE_EGL
+			bool
+			depends on LV_USE_LINUX_DRM
+
 		config LV_USE_TFT_ESPI
 			bool "Use TFT_eSPI driver"
 			default n
-- 
